ines); the bash that runs on a host is 186 lines under its ceiling plus install and bootstrap. About 29k lines of test shell test Rust programs from outside.\n\nIn order:\n\n1. #2589 Tests of Rust code live in Rust (AGENTS.md, a person's change)\n2. #2590 A ceiling on the shell of test/\n3. #2591 Port the dispatch shell tests (13.5k lines)\n4. #2592 work, #2593 cycle, #2594 update, #2595 status (16k lines)\n5. #2596 The logic of install.sh and bootstrap.sh into Rust\n\n## For 2.0 (added 2026-11-22)\n\nSteps 1 to 4 are done: `test/` is down to 49,271 lines. About 22k lines of it still test Rust programs from outside. These land on `refactor/coding-standard-v2` before the trio tag, as step T15 of the v2 plan. Cases that stub gh move onto the port fakes after T4; each issue says which of its files can land now:\n\n6. #2816 clean, stop, tidy (3.5k)\n7. #2817 the small control verbs (1.8k)\n8. #2818 plan and the headless runner (1.7k)\n9. #2819 the previews, and the Protolab plumbing T14 (#2826) keeps\n10. #2820 dev, index, mcp (2k; rule 4)\n11. #2821 the JSON contract and the read-out verbs (3.6k)\n12. #2822 state, disk, slice, the store (3k)\n13. #2823 no single slow file holds up the run (108 s now, aim under 45 s)\n14. #2824 trim the shell that stays, last\n\nFeatures that leave core in 2.0 (T16) are not ported: their shell tests go with their code.\n\n\nThe ports should take shell to about 17% of the repository.\n\n\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tehas-app/tehas-factory/issues/2597/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tehas-app/tehas-factory/issues/2597/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}
